# This project is Windows-only and ships PowerShell scripts and .txt docs that carry a
# UTF-8 BOM on purpose: Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads a .ps1/.txt without a BOM as ANSI,
# and the Chinese text in them turns to mojibake.
#
# So git is told to touch nothing: no CRLF normalisation, no encoding conversion.
# A checkout then reproduces the working tree byte-for-byte, BOM included. Do not add
# `working-tree-encoding` or per-type `text` rules here - either would tempt git into
# rewriting (and possibly stripping BOMs from) the very files that must not change.
* -text

*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.zip binary
